      "message": "Discussed over chat. I was confused about the variables. `colorBufferLatestUse` is actually either \"when the original fence signals\" in the case of no colorbuffers GL-\u003eVK syncs or \"when the GL-\u003eVK syncs finished\" because of the \n\n```\nif (releasedColorBuffers.empty()) {\n   colorBufferLatestUse \u003d queueCompletedWaitable;\n} else {\n   colorBufferLatestUse \u003d isFenceWaitable;\n}\n```\n\nblock avove so this is change seems correct. \n\n\nI think we want more change after this one to re-organize a little:\n\n```\n\u003cdevice op builder setup\u003e\n\n\u003cqueue submit and error check\u003e\n\nstd::shared_future\u003cvoid\u003e originalSubmitCompleted \u003d builder.OnQueueSubmittedWithFence(usedFence);\n\nstd::shared_future\u003cvoid\u003e allWorkCompletedWaitable \u003d originalSubmitCompletedWaitable;\n\nif (!releasedColorBuffers) {\n  allWorkCompletedWaitable \u003d scheduleAsyncWork(); \n}\n\n\u003cupdate setColorBufferLatestUse\u003e\n\u003cupdate image layouts\u003e\n\u003cupdate semaphore info\u003e\n\u003cupdate fence info\u003e\n```\n\nto \n\n1) Ensure `OnQueueSubmittedWithFence()` is actually called after the submit\n\n2) Rename a couple variables and make the flow a little easier to follow (not obvious that `isFenceWaitable` actual is \"all host operations completed\"\n\n3) Update the waitable to be a `CancelableFuture` to handle problems with shutdown similar to aosp/3237181 where `SyncThread` might shutdown before the callback happens so the waitable is never triggered.",
